# Cross-origin isolation headers for header-capable static hosts.
#
# The Runno runtimes need `SharedArrayBuffer`, which browsers only expose to
# cross-origin-isolated documents. Without these headers every Run fails with
# "SharedArrayBuffer is not defined".
#
# This file is honoured by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify (and by anything using
# the `_headers` convention). GitHub Pages ignores it entirely — which is why
# the build also ships `coi-serviceworker.js` as a fallback. Where a host
# supports headers, the service worker detects that the document is already
# isolated and does nothing, so shipping both is safe.
#
# /coi-serviceworker.js is deliberately excluded from caching so a stale copy
# can never keep a broken isolation shim alive.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# The app shell should never be cached aggressively: a stale index.html can
# reference bundle hashes that no longer exist.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/coi-serviceworker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Content-hashed bundles are safe to cache forever.
/chunk-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
